From 9fcb1cb21313ec1b5b601d3945ffa6f604ccaf49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: synrais <78070154+synrais@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:28:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: drop partial interrupt IN data when a split runs
 out of time (#115)

When the complete split of an interrupt transfer still gets a NYET after
its scheduled microframes have passed, dwc2_hc_nyet_intr() gives up and
halts the channel as a transaction error. The hub may already have
taken that packet from the device, so it is lost, but for an interrupt
IN transfer urb->actual_length still counts the packets received before
it. The device's next packet is then appended to them, and the URB
completes with the start of one report joined to part of another.

Drop what the interrupt IN transfer has received so far in that case,
so the next packet starts a new transfer.
---
[Carried from MiSTer-devel/Linux-Kernel_MiSTer 9fcb1cb21 (#115) with its
context moved past 0061's cs_miss counter; the added lines are unchanged.]

 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
index 61de804..f0630d4 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
@@ -1548,6 +1548,9 @@ static void dwc2_hc_nyet_intr(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg,
 #endif
 				qtd->complete_split = 0;
 				hsotg->hcd_stats.cs_miss++;
+				if (chan->ep_type == USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_INT &&
+				    chan->ep_is_in && qtd->urb)
+					qtd->urb->actual_length = 0;
 				dwc2_halt_channel(hsotg, chan, qtd,
 						  DWC2_HC_XFER_XACT_ERR);
 				/* Todo: add support for isoc release */
